  routeNotes: 'Corrected white upper silhouette and blue corridor from 2026-11-09
    drawing. Box 2 starts on an extended 2.8-wide crown, lowered by 1.0 for a strict
    mirrored position on the white road; push it RIGHT into the new 1.16-wide pit
    at x=12.2..13.36 after yellow. Box 2 no longer starts as an automatic filler.
    Green 1 white corridor clearance 2.34. Extend white box-2 road from x=15.3 to
    x=16.4, exactly adjoining Green 2''s right platform; move box 1 farther right
    and use it to climb the unchanged 2.0 step. All objects still use the common
    axis y=6; no box snapping or level-specific mirror formula. Level 2.1 unchanged.
    Blue geometry now shares the white pit X profile (raised crown at x=12.2..13.36)
    and extended junction x=16.4. White floor heights derive from those blue tops
    plus the established box clearance, not separate unmatched constants. Blue main/right
    bodies now overlap 0.40 horizontally and 1.40 vertically; Green 1''s narrowest
    blue band is 1.40 high. Main body bottom=2.70, Green 1 notch bottom=4.70. Portal
    tops and white floors unchanged. Thicken flag ledge downwards: bottom=5.65, top=6.85.
    Initial box 3 top=5.12 leaves 0.53 overhead, less than player height 0.76. White
    island cutout derives from the exact same rect (y=5.15..6.35). Move box 3 left
    out from under this ledge before using it to ascend. BLUE hanging pillar shell
    x=16.4..18.7, y=6.1..11.9 preserves the separate box-only barrier. Lower-left
    corner meets main platform upper-right corner at (16.4,6.1), with zero horizontal
    overlap and zero vertical gap. No ceiling over box 1''s pushing area. Shell strictly
    mirrors to y=0.1..5.9 and remains BLUE; approved white route uses normal opposite-phase
    filtering.'
